A||||22||fierosound||Turbos - Kits or DIY??||||10||
Z||000000||fierosound||12-18-1999||03:53 PM||||Anyone here have a turbo'd V6?  Did you get a kit or DIY?  How'd you like it??  I found some good sites below indicating great results.<P><BR>Dennis LaGrua's turbo - <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A> <P><BR>IRM Stage II turbo install - <A HREF="http://www.ma.iup.edu/~lmmd/Turbo.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ma.iup.edu/~lmmd/Turbo.html</A> <P><BR>Turbos, parts and accessories -  <A HREF="http://www.turbocity.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.turbocity.com/</A> <P>||||reg||10
Z||000001||four50four||12-18-1999||05:31 PM||||stroker, from this forum, was in the process of manufacturing a kit. haven't heard from him in a while, though||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||12-18-1999||11:10 PM||||I too have built a kit but havent installed it yet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||12-18-1999||11:25 PM||||fierosound, I've got an IRM turbo on my 86SE. It's been in the car for at least seven years. It is the MillerWoods stage one turbo. IRM also installed the turbo. I can't imagine it would be too hard to install, but I'm not mechanically inclined! It's very reliable and runs like a bat out of hell! Any more questions feel free to ask!||||reg||1
Z||000004||cobra427||12-18-1999||11:54 PM||||does anyone in here have any comments or experience with the twin-turbo kit that IFG offered about six years ago? I need all the info that i can get. TIA||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||12-19-1999||10:28 AM||||cobra, I've heard the IFG twin-turbo kit is pretty good, it costs about $500 more than the single turbo kit. It reduces the turbo lag by spooling the first turbo (usually the smallest) up at low rpm's, then going to the second turbo above 2500 rpms. It also puts out more heat in your engine compartment. I thought about the twin turbo at one point, but the single turbo is all I need, it's probably easier on the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000006||loafer87gt||12-19-1999||02:39 PM||||I heard the IFG TT had a lot of problems. They were running too much boost and the chip was very optimized so the engine would more or less self destruct. It put 375 horses if I remember correctly though. I tried to get a hold of them a couple months ago, but couldn;t get a hold of anyone. They are making turbos for Mr2's and imports now. If someone could get one of their kits and get the PROm properly program and have the engine built to a lower compression ratio to handle the boost one of these kits might be fun. I have an article in my FOCOA magazine if someone wants me to scan it in.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||12-19-1999||04:25 PM||||I have the broschure for the I.F.G. twin turbo. I called them way back in 92 or 93 and they sent me the papers. The look of the kit is very impressive.||||reg||1
Z||000008||cobra427||12-19-1999||07:53 PM||||Thanks to SCCA FIERO and loafer87gt. This is exactly the kind of info that i am looking for. My reason being that, i got a system very similar to the IFG. The differences being, this kit used TDO4 mitsubishi's turbos.It has all the plumbing minus the final exhaust piping (thats no big deal tho).I have talked to Kevim Leslie about using his stage II system plus the two atmostphere MAP sensor. That will solve some of the problems i'm sure Heat dssipation will be another obsacle to overcome not to mention engine strenght as well. So if you gentlemen would be so kind as to send me any info you have, I would be much obliged.<BR>Please send to:  cobra@c4.net or snail-mail me at:<BR>      Jody Lemos<BR>      PO Box977<BR>      East Orleans,Ma.02643<BR>TIA<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||four50four||12-19-1999||08:39 PM||||loafer, i would be interested in seeing the article. its just for my personal interest, so if its any trouble don't bother.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||12-19-1999||11:46 PM||||a twin turbo Fiero is something I've been interested by for a while, so if you get the stuff scanned, I wouldn't mind a copy also!<P>  <A HREF="mailto:fiero@digitalfusion.on.ca">fiero@digitalfusion.on.ca</A>  <P>No rush tho, it's just something I think would be cool to look at.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-19-1999).]||||reg||1
