Z||000017||kong||12-20-1999||09:03 PM||||Hello everyone! Can you put a turbo on a 2.5 with TBI? I know where I can get one off a ford t-bird for a good price. Has anyone bothered to put one on the lowly 4 banger? And if so how did they like it?||||reg||5
Z||000018||ChadMan||12-21-1999||08:39 AM||||Kong, you might want to buy the Brooklands "Fiero" book and read about the Pfaff Turbo kit from 1984.  I remember it made about 140 hp and went 0-60 in around 8 sec - about what an unblown V6 will do.<P>With good-running V6 cars out there for $1200 and up, I can't imagine it being worth the effort to turbo the 4 unless you really love your car and/or you want a unique Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000019||kong||12-22-1999||08:50 PM||||Hey Chadman,   I would like to have another Fiero (v-6) but I have no place to put it. All my parking space is already used up. Besides I am the kind to have something different(And I'm almost broke!lol).  Anyway I can get the whole turbo outfit for $50.00 from a friend before he junks the car. (His wife wrecked it). And i have access to a well equiped shop where I/or friends can fabricate what I need. Just looking for something to do this winter besides watching tv and going nuts||||reg||6
Z||000020||william_thorniii||12-22-1999||09:37 PM||||Kong, <P>I know that the turbo's from T'birds work in this application.  I think that it is the Garett T2 or T3.  There is a guy on the fiero-list that has added a turbocharger to his L-4.  I haven't heard any feedback from him lately, so I don't know if he ever got it working right or not.  The problem is that you need a many other parts other than the turbo.  Your best bet is to probably find a late 80's Turbo sunbird in the boneyard.  I am guesstimating here... Then you need to pull the ECM, wiring harness (not necessary, but will probably make it easier) and associated sensors (maf, map?).  Then you need to create a custom exhaust with which you can route the necessary air.  Don't forget to pull the intercooler and wastegate off of the T-bird too.  For home grown V-6 turbo projects, check out Dennis LaGrua's webpage (sorry don't have the URL).  He goes through an entire turbo project from bone-yard to Fiero.<P>Hope this helps,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000021||kong||12-23-1999||10:32 PM||||Thanks Thorn I'll see if I can find it. You can never have too much information.||||reg||1
Z||000022||four50four||12-23-1999||11:42 PM||||the URL is at the top of this thread||||reg||6
Z||000023||SCCA FIERO||12-24-1999||12:22 AM||||My turbo came from an 87 Ford T-Bird and is an IHI turbo. This turbo is water-cooled and the older Garretts are not. The turbo and intercooler set me back a whopping $50. I also have my Y pipe just no time to fiddle with it.||||reg||1
